+# Experiment G2 Result
+
+## Change
+
+- `src/cascade.rs`: `exec` now returns `Result<u64, DbErr>`, forwarding
+  `ExecResult::rows_affected()`.
+- The `assert` and both `retract_dred` BFS passes retain `DELETE FROM cx_next;
+  INSERT INTO cx_next ...` statement order and use the final INSERT's returned
+  affected-row count to terminate a round.
+- Removed the `SELECT count(*) FROM cx_next` probe from those three loops.
+- `retract`, `retract_dred_cte`, and other crates were not changed.
+- Acyclic fast path: not attempted.
+
+## Validation
+
+`cargo build --release --example perf_report` completed:
+
+```
+Finished `release` profile [optimized] target(s) in 18.37s
+```
+
+The required commands use widths `160000` and `480000`. Their emitted RESULT
+counts were `800002` and `2400001`, respectively. Each run used
+`DL_MEMCAP_MB=2048`.
+
+| Brief scale | RESULT count | Before ms range | After ms range | Before stmts | After stmts | out_hash before = after |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| 960k (`6 160000 0`) | 800002 | 2039.927 to 2048.188 | 2044.222 to 2051.511 | 75 | 71 | `dd6a707234617ea5` |
+| 2.9M (`6 480000 0`) | 2400001 | 6322.907 to 6498.569 | 6308.882 to 6325.692 | 75 | 71 | `454c5271a7e5a260` |
+
+Both output hashes equal their corresponding baseline hash. The statement-count
+delta is minus 4 on this graph shape. The 960k timing ranges overlap; the 2.9M
+after range is lower than the before range.
